hat.com/images/video-off.gif\" height=\"30\" class=\"k\" alt=\"video\"></a>\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"#\"><img src=\"https://blackhat.com/images/audio-off.gif\" height=\"30\" class=\"k\" alt=\"audio\"></a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://blackhat.com/presentations/bh-europe-09/Smith/BlackHat-Europe-2009-Smith-VAASeline-VNC-Attack-whitepaper.pdf\"><img src=\"https://blackhat.com/images/presentation.gif\" height=\"30\" class=\"k\" alt=\"presentation\"></a>\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://blackhat.com/presentations/bh-europe-09/Smith/BlackHat-Europe-2009-Smith-VAASeline-VNC-Attack-slides.pdf\"><img src=\"https://blackhat.com/images/ppt.gif\" height=\"30\" class=\"k\" alt=\"ppt\"></a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<a name=\"Temmingh\"></a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<h2>Roelof Temmingh and Chris Bohme</h2>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<h3>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tIntegrating Maltego with Offensive and Defensive Open Source Tools\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</h3>\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<hr>\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"#\"><img src=\"https://blackhat.com/images/video-off.gif\" height=\"30\" class=\"k\" alt=\"video\"></a>\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"#\"><img src=\"https://blackhat.com/images/audio-off.gif\" height=\"30\" class=\"k\" alt=\"audio\"></a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"#\"><img src=\"https://blackhat.com/images/presentation-off.gif\" height=\"30\" class=\"k\" alt=\"presentation\"></a>\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://blackhat.com/presentations/bh-europe-09/Temmingh_Brohme/blackhat-europe-2009-temmingh-brohme-maltego-slides.pdf\"><img src=\"https://blackhat.com/images/ppt.gif\" height=\"30\" class=\"k\" alt=\"ppt\"></a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<a name=\"Vanbeek\"></a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<h2>Jeroen van Beek</h2>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<h3>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tPassports Reloaded Goes Mobile \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</h3>\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<hr>\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"#\"><img src=\"https://blackhat.com/images/video-off.gif\" height=\"30\" class=\"k\" alt=\"video\"></a>\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"#\"><img src=\"https://blackhat.com/images/audio-off.gif\" height=\"30\" class=\"k\" alt=\"audio\"></a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://blackhat.com/presentations/bh-europe-09/VanBeek/BlackHat-Europe-2009-VanBeek-ePassports-Mobile.pdf\"><img src=\"https://blackhat.com/images/presentation.gif\" height=\"30\" class=\"k\" alt=\"presentation\"></a>\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://blackhat.com/presentations/bh-europe-09/VanBeek/BlackHat-Europe-2009-VanBeek-ePassports-Mobile-slides.pdf\"><img src=\"https://blackhat.com/images/ppt.gif\" height=\"30\" class=\"k\" alt=\"ppt\"></a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<!--<div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<a name=\"Weinmann\"></a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<h2>Ralf-Philipp Weinmann </h2>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<h3>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<strong>Alternate: </strong>Instantaneous Cloning of DECT Handsets Over the Air\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</h3>\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<p>\n\nThe Digital Enhanced Cordless Telephony standard has not been subject to security research for almost 15 years. Recently, the deDECTed.org team reverse-engineered the two proprietary symmetric key primitives used in DECT, the DECT Standard Cipher and the DECT Standard Authentication Algorithm and presented cheap and viable methods for sniffing and intercepting DECT phone calls.</p>\n\n<p>In this talk we demonstrate methods to clone DECT handsets over the air by simply sniffing two challenge/response pairs. This is achieved by exploiting a combination of a protocol flaw and various implementation flaws in the key allocation process. By reverse-engineering various lines of DECT stacks, we found a variety of weaknesses in their respective PRNGs. All of them are practically exploitable. Using a time/memory tradeoff, we can perform the attacks instantaneously.</p>\n\n<p>Information about the Pairing (IPEI of the handset, RFPI of the base station, UAK) usually are stored in an serial EEPROM in DECT handsets. We will show how to modify this with only a minimal amount of hardware, also giving examples of phones where this EEPROM can be directly reprogrammed via the keypad.</p>\n\n<p>A live demonstration of the attack will be given and the differences between residential and corporate DECT installations will be discussed. We will also demonstrate how to decrypt encrypted conversations once the UAK has been recovered.\n</p>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"evenbox\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<p class=\"black\"><span>Ralf-Philipp Weinmann</span>  is a cryptologist by day, and a reverse-engineer by night. He has studied and obtained his Ph.D. at the Technical University of Darmstadt and is currently researching as a post-doc at the LACS laboratory of the University of Luxembourg. He refuses to accept \"this algorithm is under NDA\" as an excuse to refrain from cryptanalyzing an algorithm, but he has never signed one. The putrid smell of proprietary crypto algorithms attracts him like a piece of dead meat in the desert attracts a vulture. Also, he is a real aficionado of skewed random distributions and broken crypto implementations.</p>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>-->\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<a name=\"Wysopal\"></a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<h2>Chris Wysopal</h2>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<h3>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tDetecting \"Certified Pre-owned\" Software and Devices\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</h3>\n<hr>\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"#\"><img src=\"https://blackhat.com/images/video-off.gif\" height=\"30\" class=\"k\" alt=\"video\"></a>\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"#\"><img src=\"https://blackhat.com/images/audio-off.gif\" height=\"30\" class=\"k\" alt=\"audio\"></a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://blackhat.com/presentations/bh-europe-09/Wysopal/BlackHat-Europe-2009-Wysopal-Certified-Pre-Owned-1.00-wp.pdf\"><img src=\"https://blackhat.com/images/presentation.gif\" height=\"30\" class=\"k\" alt=\"presentation\"></a>\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://blackhat.com/presentations/bh-europe-09/Wysopal/BlackHat-Europe-2009-Wysopal-Certified-Pre-Owned-1.00-slides.pdf\"><img src=\"https://blackhat.com/images/ppt.gif\" height=\"30\" class=\"k\" alt=\"ppt\"></a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<a name=\"Zanero\"></a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<h2>Stefano Zanero &amp; Claudio Criscione</h2>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<h3>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tMasibty: a Web Application Firewall Based on Anomaly Detection\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</h3>\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<hr>\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"#\"><img src=\"https://blackhat.com/images/video-off.gif\" height=\"30\" class=\"k\" alt=\"video\"></a>\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"#\"><img src=\"https://blackhat.com/images/audio-off.gif\" height=\"30\" class=\"k\" alt=\"audio\"></a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://blackhat.com/presentations/bh-europe-09/Zanero_Criscione/BlackHat-Europe-2009-Zanero-Criscione-Masibty-Web-App-Firewall-wp.pdf\"><img src=\"https://blackhat.com/images/presentation-off.gif\" height=\"30\" class=\"k\" alt=\"presentation\"></a>\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://blackhat.com/presentations/bh-europe-09/Zanero_Criscione/BlackHat-Europe-2009-Zanero-Criscione-Masibty-Web-App-Firewall-slides.pdf\"><img src=\"https://blackhat.com/images/ppt.gif\" height=\"30\" class=\"k\" alt=\"ppt\"></a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"column span-24\">\n\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t</div>\n\n\n    </div>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"column span-24\">\n     \n    </div>\n  </div>\